WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.866 --> 00:00:10.433
A long, long time ago,

2
00:00:10.866 --> 00:00:13.533
a time recalled through Kalos legend...

3
00:00:18.433 --> 00:00:19.500
No, wait.

4
00:00:20.666 --> 00:00:22.066
Jan, please don't go.

5
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.566
Aila, I promise you I will defeat Yveltal.

6
00:00:25.633 --> 00:00:27.566
Have faith and wait for me.

7
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.566
Talonflame, go!

8
00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:34.533
Please.

9
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.566
Jan, no!

10
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:44.900
And so, a young man embarked on a journey, leaving his beloved behind.

11
00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:48.800
His target, the Destruction Pokémon, Yveltal.

12
00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:01.866
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

13
00:01:01.933 --> 00:01:05.900
♪ Knock me down, I'll just get up again ♪

14
00:01:05.966 --> 00:01:09.100
♪ You've met your match Yeah, I'm no beginner ♪

15
00:01:09.166 --> 00:01:11.000
♪ Pokémon ♪

16
00:01:11.066 --> 00:01:13.466
- ♪ Pokémon ♪
- ♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

17
00:01:13.533 --> 00:01:16.733
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

18
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.733
♪ Pokémon ♪

19
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.600
- ♪ Pokémon ♪
- ♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

20
00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.333
The Maiden Statue.

21
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.333
Hey. Alexa.

22
00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.333
Hmm? Hi, Professor Sycamore.

23
00:01:55.866 --> 00:01:58.433
Are you here to investigate the ruins, too?

24
00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:01.833
Well, it is the biggest find of the century.

25
00:02:02.533 --> 00:02:05.866
The ruins that confirm the truth of a Kalos legend.

26
00:02:07.833 --> 00:02:10.766
Who knew they'd be found at such a high altitude?

27
00:02:10.833 --> 00:02:14.900
Right. It's amazing they were never discovered until now.

28
00:02:15.333 --> 00:02:17.400
So, where is the Maiden Statue?

29
00:02:17.866 --> 00:02:19.566
Come. I'll show you.

30
00:02:23.333 --> 00:02:28.033
You see, it was accidentally discovered on a satellite image.

31
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:31.433
A temple-like structure overgrown by nature.

32
00:02:32.333 --> 00:02:34.533
Because the location is treacherous,

33
00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.533
it took some time to get a research team up here.

34
00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.566
Why did you accompany the research team, Alexa?

35
00:02:41.933 --> 00:02:43.200
Because of this.

36
00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.066
Through the discovery of various artifacts,

37
00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:49.566
we knew there was an ancient nation that flourished here,

38
00:02:49.633 --> 00:02:53.466
which ultimately became the foundation of civilization in Kalos.

39
00:02:54.433 --> 00:02:56.266
I wanted to report on the lives

40
00:02:56.333 --> 00:02:59.100
of the people and Pokémon living at that time.

41
00:03:10.833 --> 00:03:11.666
That's it.

42
00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:18.533
The statue of Aila, the stone-eyed maiden, as described in Kalos legend.

43
00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:24.633
It's as though someone took a moment of her life and carved it into stone.

44
00:03:26.333 --> 00:03:28.900
Exactly as the legend describes.

45
00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.366
- Ancient historical records?
- That's right.

46
00:03:35.733 --> 00:03:40.466
And we've come to know this segment as the chapter of the stone-eyed maiden.

47
00:03:41.366 --> 00:03:43.566
Her hair, her necklace.

48
00:03:44.533 --> 00:03:49.033
Everything written within these records perfectly matches the statue.

49
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:55.733
For the longest time, people debated whether what's written here took place,

50
00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:59.600
or if it was simply fabricated by someone during ancient times.

51
00:04:00.933 --> 00:04:04.600
Now we have the statue, so, we may finally get the answer.

52
00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:09.133
This statue wasn't a figment of someone's imagination?

53
00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:14.166
Don't you think that it's possible that someone created it based on these records?

54
00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.200
That can't be ruled out. However...

55
00:04:18.333 --> 00:04:19.633
her expression...

56
00:04:20.233 --> 00:04:23.033
I don't think that this is any ordinary statue.

57
00:04:24.266 --> 00:04:27.700
I believe the stone-eyed maiden actually existed.

58
00:04:28.166 --> 00:04:32.133
And the one who turned her into stone is none other than Yveltal,

59
00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.200
the Destruction Pokémon.

60
00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:37.700
Yveltal?

61
00:04:38.666 --> 00:04:41.633
Based on all the research conducted up until now,

62
00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:46.433
it is believed that this symbol resembling a Y is a reference to Yveltal

63
00:04:46.633 --> 00:04:48.700
in all the drawings we have of it.

64
00:04:49.133 --> 00:04:52.700
Those drawings and this symbol look the same to me.

65
00:04:52.766 --> 00:04:56.566
The story begins when two people from different social classes,

66
00:04:56.633 --> 00:05:00.266
a poor man named Jan and Aila, the village chief's daughter,

67
00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.366
meet and fall in love.

68
00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:08.866
At the time, the city's oracle, Olympica, made a prediction.

69
00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.266
Yes.

70
00:05:10.333 --> 00:05:11.400
I see it.

71
00:05:11.966 --> 00:05:14.666
Yveltal will descend upon this land,

72
00:05:15.233 --> 00:05:18.000
absorbing the life force of all living things.

73
00:05:18.066 --> 00:05:20.166
Yveltal's life will come to an end

74
00:05:20.233 --> 00:05:23.233
and then it will turn into a cocoon once more.

75
00:05:23.566 --> 00:05:27.233
It is, however, impossible for any of us to escape this fate.

76
00:05:27.566 --> 00:05:30.233
When Aila's father learned of this prophecy,

77
00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:34.500
he ordered Jan to defeat Yveltal in order to protect the city.

78
00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:40.933
He promised his daughter's hand in marriage if Jan defeated Yveltal.

79
00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:46.333
You don't have to listen to my father and his promise.

80
00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.800
Yveltal is extremely dangerous. You can't defeat it.

81
00:05:49.966 --> 00:05:52.900
No one can defeat it. Don't even try.

82
00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:55.933
Jan, please don't go. I'm begging you.

83
00:05:56.366 --> 00:06:01.500
Aila, I promise you I will defeat Yveltal. Have faith and wait for me.

84
00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:08.533
-Huh?

85
00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:11.800
It's Yveltal!

86
00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:13.800
Aila!

87
00:06:14.233 --> 00:06:16.066
Jan, stay away!

88
00:06:19.233 --> 00:06:20.800
Talonflame!

89
00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:35.500
Why, you...

90
00:06:38.433 --> 00:06:39.666
Jan!

91
00:06:58.666 --> 00:07:02.633
- What happened to Yveltal after that?
- Like the prediction said,

92
00:07:02.866 --> 00:07:05.266
it changed its shape into a cocoon.

93
00:07:06.766 --> 00:07:11.066
It absorbed all life sources around it and the land became barren,

94
00:07:11.633 --> 00:07:14.100
so, it could enter its long slumber.

95
00:07:39.366 --> 00:07:42.166
Aila leaped between Yveltal and Jan, then.

96
00:07:46.866 --> 00:07:47.700
Aila.

97
00:07:54.833 --> 00:07:56.933
Do we know where Yveltal is now?

98
00:07:57.466 --> 00:08:01.000
One theory states it awakens every thousand years, but...

99
00:08:01.066 --> 00:08:04.800
it's uncertain if Yveltal's now a cocoon, or awake and active.

100
00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:20.566
The precious few people and Pokémon who survived have left this land.

101
00:08:21.266 --> 00:08:23.300
I'm leaving this land, too.

102
00:08:25.833 --> 00:08:27.866
How could this have taken place?

103
00:08:28.933 --> 00:08:31.733
There's only one chance of rescuing the girl.

104
00:08:33.299 --> 00:08:35.866
Perhaps Xerneas is able to bring her back.

105
00:08:36.433 --> 00:08:37.466
Xerneas?

106
00:08:37.733 --> 00:08:40.966
Yveltal's equal. The Life Pokémon.

107
00:08:41.266 --> 00:08:46.866
When Xerneas transforms into a large tree, it shares its power with the land,

108
00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:51.366
and that sharing can bring even the most barren of lands back to life.

109
00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:53.866
So, do you know where Xerneas is?

110
00:08:56.866 --> 00:08:59.866
Find a forest that glimmers like a rainbow.

111
00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:03.433
Wherever Xerneas is, that forest flourishes.

112
00:09:06.666 --> 00:09:08.533
So, the symbol X...

113
00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:12.966
- It's a reference to Xerneas, isn't it?
- Yes, that's right.

114
00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:19.400
Jan visited many lush forests.

115
00:09:19.633 --> 00:09:22.566
But because Xerneas is constantly on the move,

116
00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:26.200
sadly, Jan wasn't ever able to find it.

117
00:09:29.066 --> 00:09:31.800
And time passed mercilessly.

118
00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:36.333
What?

119
00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:39.000
We can't stop.

120
00:09:39.333 --> 00:09:41.466
We need to find where Xerneas is.

121
00:09:53.766 --> 00:09:54.633
Huh?

122
00:10:00.933 --> 00:10:03.533
The forest. It's lifeless.

123
00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:09.966
Is it Yveltal?

124
00:10:12.566 --> 00:10:14.333
It's terrible, isn't it?

125
00:10:16.566 --> 00:10:18.466
Can you tell me what happened?

126
00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:21.966
His people came, and then he took Xerneas away.

127
00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:23.500
Xerneas?

128
00:10:24.533 --> 00:10:26.500
Who's that Pokémon?

129
00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:33.500
It's Yveltal!

130
00:10:38.033 --> 00:10:40.233
The one who took Xerneas away

131
00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:42.866
turned out to be the ruler of a small kingdom.

132
00:10:43.733 --> 00:10:44.666
His goal?

133
00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:48.166
He tried to monopolize the Life Pokémon's power

134
00:10:48.333 --> 00:10:50.533
for his own selfish purposes.

135
00:10:51.433 --> 00:10:56.300
So, because Xerneas was taken away, the forest turned barren and brown?

136
00:10:57.033 --> 00:11:00.833
Yes, and all due to one man's selfish actions.

137
00:11:12.033 --> 00:11:13.733
What is going on?

138
00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:17.766
I brought Xerneas to my garden, yet nothing is flourishing.

139
00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:23.966
So, bestowing eternal life is nothing more than a worthless illusion, Xerneas?

140
00:11:26.033 --> 00:11:27.700
Set it on fire.

141
00:11:27.766 --> 00:11:32.100
- Are you sure of it?
- Do it. It is of no worth to me.

142
00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:36.200
And if it brings me no benefit, burn it.

143
00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:37.466
Let's go.

144
00:11:45.533 --> 00:11:47.466
Stop it!

145
00:11:52.666 --> 00:11:54.433
You have no right to be here.

146
00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:57.500
- Put out that fire!
- Silence!

147
00:11:57.566 --> 00:12:00.766
No, release Xerneas and extinguish the fire at once!

148
00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:04.966
Xerneas belongs to me. I will do whatever I want with it.

149
00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:07.933
Don't you feel anything seeing it burning?

150
00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:11.266
Making Xerneas suffer will bring misfortune and pain!

151
00:12:11.333 --> 00:12:13.100
Such utter nonsense.

152
00:12:13.166 --> 00:12:15.733
- Get rid of this man at once!
- Sir.

153
00:12:27.866 --> 00:12:31.800
Stop! There's nothing to worry about! You must remain calm!

154
00:12:46.466 --> 00:12:49.200
What in the world is that thing?

155
00:12:53.766 --> 00:12:56.400
So, at that moment, Zygarde appeared?

156
00:12:56.866 --> 00:12:57.700
Yes.

157
00:12:58.266 --> 00:13:01.933
This symbol resembling a Z is a reference to Zygarde.

158
00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:10.666
Zygarde, the Order Pokémon.

159
00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:13.800
Zygarde watches over Kalos' ecological system

160
00:13:13.866 --> 00:13:17.700
and unleashes its fury on those who try to destroy that system.

161
00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:39.366
It's like the human immune system.

162
00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:43.700
It heal irregularities in the body and bring it back into balance.

163
00:13:44.133 --> 00:13:44.966
You're right.

164
00:13:45.033 --> 00:13:49.033
Zygarde is also known throughout the land as the watcher of Kalos.

165
00:13:49.733 --> 00:13:52.366
It eradicates harmful situations.

166
00:14:15.933 --> 00:14:16.966
Xerneas.

167
00:14:18.433 --> 00:14:22.466
I'm begging you to assist me. Come to my aid with your great power.

168
00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:28.733
Wait! Xerneas!

169
00:14:56.033 --> 00:14:59.066
At that moment, Jan came to a realization.

170
00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:02.066
He knew that the land destroyed by Yveltal

171
00:15:02.133 --> 00:15:05.200
would someday become even more lush and alive.

172
00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:11.300
So, he made the decision to protect the land alongside Aila.

173
00:15:18.466 --> 00:15:22.433
It's said Jan recorded everything that he saw and experienced.

174
00:15:24.866 --> 00:15:27.866
And that's what has been passed down to us.

175
00:15:28.833 --> 00:15:32.000
After a very long time, the land became plagued

176
00:15:32.066 --> 00:15:33.600
by a devastating drought.

177
00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:40.333
And once again, it became savagely barren and devoid of life.

178
00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:47.100
Dear Gogoat.

179
00:15:48.433 --> 00:15:49.266
Huh?

180
00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:00.900
Xerneas, you have come.

181
00:16:51.766 --> 00:16:52.600
Aila.

182
00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:15.333
Unfortunately, according to legend,

183
00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:17.833
Aila never returned to her original state.

184
00:17:18.900 --> 00:17:22.566
I believe both Xerneas and Yveltal are incarnations of nature

185
00:17:22.633 --> 00:17:24.266
that take care of the land.

186
00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:26.766
That is their task and their purpose.

187
00:17:26.933 --> 00:17:32.866
And when the natural order is undone, Zygarde appears in order to balance it.

188
00:17:34.333 --> 00:17:39.033
These three powerful Pokémon preside over the never-ending cycle of life.

189
00:17:40.066 --> 00:17:42.733
And perhaps, there is a distinct possibility

190
00:17:42.800 --> 00:17:46.033
that Zygarde Cells could be watching over us right now.

191
00:17:47.533 --> 00:17:49.933
Zygarde Cells are not normally seen.

192
00:17:50.166 --> 00:17:53.100
However, they are everywhere in the Kalos region.

193
00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:59.133
That was clearly proven during the incident involving Team Flare.

194
00:18:03.433 --> 00:18:06.166
Any idea what happened to Jan after that?

195
00:18:06.233 --> 00:18:10.666
No. The legend doesn't mention anything having to do with Jan's fate.

196
00:18:12.666 --> 00:18:15.166
That means only she knows.

197
00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:18.200
There is another possibility.

198
00:18:19.100 --> 00:18:21.400
Perhaps Zygarde was watching, too.

199
00:18:24.466 --> 00:18:27.133
Can you please show me the rest of the ruins?

200
00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:30.633
Yeah. Sure. I'll introduce you to the research team.

201
00:18:31.066 --> 00:18:33.633
Thanks very much. I'm so glad I came here.

202
00:18:58.000 --> 00:18:58.866
Huh?

203
00:19:01.666 --> 00:19:02.866
Oh, dear me!

204
00:19:05.066 --> 00:19:06.366
Can I help you?

205
00:19:09.066 --> 00:19:09.966
Hello.

206
00:19:11.166 --> 00:19:13.866
Do you always take a nap right here, sir?

207
00:19:14.833 --> 00:19:20.100
Young lady, I was just having a conversation with this woman.

208
00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:22.233
A conversation?

209
00:19:22.666 --> 00:19:26.733
Yes. I was telling her that thanks to a Pokémon named Xerneas,

210
00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:30.166
the season when flowers bloom is upon us once again.

211
00:19:30.233 --> 00:19:32.233
You mean the Legendary Pokémon?

212
00:19:32.666 --> 00:19:36.966
A long, long time ago, this old man actually met Xerneas.

213
00:19:37.466 --> 00:19:41.400
- You're kidding, right?
- Oh, no, I speak the truth.

214
00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:45.033
I met Yveltal, too, and I also met a third.

215
00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:49.766
A green-colored Pokémon shaped something like this.

216
00:19:50.966 --> 00:19:55.400
- Wow, amazing.
- The forest stays lush and beautiful,

217
00:19:55.466 --> 00:19:59.066
thanks to the caring and watchful eyes of all three of them.

218
00:19:59.966 --> 00:20:03.400
Won't you come back to my house and tell me more stories?

219
00:20:05.033 --> 00:20:07.466
I don't want to leave this place.

220
00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:11.033
- Do you want to stay because of her?
- Yes.

221
00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:15.600
And here I will always remain.

222
00:20:21.866 --> 00:20:24.000
Now, I must return to my nap.

223
00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:26.966
Thank you for the conversation, young lady.

224
00:20:27.033 --> 00:20:28.866
It was most enjoyable.

225
00:20:32.133 --> 00:20:34.833
Xerneas, Yveltal and Zygarde.

226
00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:39.066
Those three will continue to watch over Kalos and its history,

227
00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:42.100
along with the statue of the stone-eyed maiden.
